M (red) cut-offs are strict less-than, and MAM (yellow) lower\nbounds are inclusive (>=), matching the guideline's own boundary\nconvention -- a MUAC value exactly at a cut-off (e.g. 13.5 for the\n5-<10y bracket) classifies as MAM/yellow, not SAM/red.\n\nReference example verified: a 5-year-old with MUAC 13.0cm now\ncorrectly classifies as red/SAM.\n\n* test(vitals): O3-5957 parameterize MUAC boundary tests\n\nConverts the boundary-age tests to a single test.each table covering\nall five age brackets at their red/yellow/green cut-offs, including\nthe under-5 bracket and the green case, which weren't covered before.","authorName":"Faisal Mehmood","authorEmail":"sfm7776@gmail.com"},{"hash":"bda2ce4aac69061ef4db6b45c88455f8cbd30e4c","date":"2026-05-13T19:56:26+03:00","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#3301)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d4857fbf84af21943b989c91c1b37277ff3ff2fd","date":"2026-04-17T16:01:13+03:00","message":"(feat) Surface BMI reference ranges in the biometrics table (#3238)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"3e58d3eb4e079c4d530e105dcd963f034e4f9271","date":"2026-03-13T14:12:15+01:00","message":"(feat) O3-5364: Add configurable minimum age for displaying BMI (#2914)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Oliver Lewandowski","authorEmail":"109145288+olewandowski1@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"b2270525c8afea42e924e28916c44fa398fef91c","date":"2026-03-09T18:30:10+03:00","message":"(fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty (#3084)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty\n\nJavaScript treats 0 as falsy, which caused zero-valued vitals to be\nsilently skipped across the entire pipeline — fetching, display,\nflagging, validation, and persistence.\n\nReplace all truthiness checks (if (value), Boolean(value), value && ...)\nwith explicit null checks (value != null && value !== '') so that 0 is\ntreated as a real recorded value while undefined, null, and empty strings\ncontinue to mean \"no value\".\n\nAffected layers:\n- assessValue: 0 is now evaluated against reference ranges and flagged\n- prepareObsForSubmission: 0-valued obs are created; editing to 0 no\n  longer voids the old obs without creating a replacement\n- data.resource: 0-valued FHIR observations are no longer dropped from\n  the encounter hash table\n- VitalsHeaderItem: 0 displays with its unit instead of \"Not available\"\n- vitals-header.extension: unit symbols render for 0-valued vitals\n- Form workspace: interpretation and range validation run for 0 values\n- Schema: a form with only a 0-valued field passes \"at least one field\"\n- Input validity: typing 0 is no longer flagged as invalid input\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback: null-check range thresholds and MUAC conditional\n\n- assessValue: use != null for range threshold checks (hiCritical,\n  hiNormal, lowCritical, lowNormal) so a threshold of 0 is not skipped\n- vitals header: use != null for MUAC conditional rendering for\n  consistency with the rest of the patch","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"0599558fdb8e2c2ab990f688b8f019f1559187da","date":"2026-02-11T22:23:50+03:00","message":"(fix) Derive unsaved changes from dirtyFields instead of isDirty in vitals form (#3012)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"e7ee451c31e8d2d388a286c16ccbfeae3afc76b8","date":"2026-01-20T23:42:17-05:00","message":"(test) update workspace props in unit tests (#2958)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"9465b6b181bd8e5385cf418b09fcf7a172a1d590","date":"2026-01-05T17:45:17+03:00","message":"(chore) Upgrade TypeScript ESLint to v8 and fix type issues (#2913)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"1cae1653b6f2aa4435310ac356e4170778eb64d0","date":"2025-12-04T08:57:33-05:00","message":"(BREAKING) O3-4961 Workspace v2 migration (#2800)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-4962 store visitContext in patient chart store\n\n* fix immunization-from test failure\n\n* add missing changes\n\n* add e2e test for visit context\n\n* clear visit context when ending or deleting active visit\n\n* migrate visit-context-switcher to use patinet chart store\n\n* fix visit context unset incorrectly when ending active visit\n\n* (BREAKING) Workspace v2 migration\n\n* address PR feedback\n\n* add e2e test steps for visit context when deleting and restoring active visit\n\n* fix unit tests\n\n* fix e2e tests\n\n* update esm-core and fix order basket\n\n* add exported workspaces\n\n* remove unused cancel-order-form\n\n* exported workspaces fixup\n\n* comments\n\n* migrate fill-prescription form workspace\n\n* fix NPE\n\n* fix e2e tests\n\n* address feedback\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-medications-app/src/routes.json\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"2353ca210637b8e7a1bc9ea45c52f4137577e2aa","date":"2025-11-13T07:17:44-05:00","message":"(BREAKING) O3-4962: Store visit context in patient chart store (#2669)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-4962 store visitContext in patient chart store\n\n* fix immunization-from test failure\n\n* add missing changes\n\n* add e2e test for visit context\n\n* clear visit context when ending or deleting active visit\n\n* migrate visit-context-switcher to use patinet chart store\n\n* fix visit context unset incorrectly when ending active visit\n\n* address PR feedback\n\n* add e2e test steps for visit context when deleting and restoring active visit\n\n* fix merge\n\n* Rebase","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"443f4edf40768d6c9ec169f6002138c242d5e53d","date":"2025-11-13T01:53:45+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5046: Resolve form label accessibility violations  (#2842)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) O3-5046: Resolve form label accessibility violations (O3-5046)\n\n- Remove orphaned label elements that weren't associated with form controls\n- Convert improper label usage to semantic span elements for display purposes\n- Add proper labelText content to Search components instead of empty strings\n- Implement aria-labelledby association for custom form controls\n- Fix missing labelText in patient list and visit form components\n- Add fallback chain for concept display names in lab results\n- Ensure all form controls have accessible labels for WCAG 2.1 compliance","authorName":"Raj Prakash","authorEmail":"rjnt452@gmail.com"},{"hash":"e359da592c220eecde4552ad213e4bc2cdd8e195","date":"2025-07-04T09:41:45+03:00","message":"(feat) Optimize visit data revalidation to avoid SWR cache cascades (#2554)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Optimize visit data revalidation to avoid SWR cache cascades\n\nThis PR addresses performance bottlenecks in visit and encounter data management by replacing global revalidation with more targeted cache invalidation.\n\nPresently, the global `mutateVisit()` revalidation function triggers 13+ unnecessary network requests per operation, and all visit-related components are revalidated even when only specific data changed.\n\nThis approach:\n\n- Replaces the global `mutateVisit()` with targeted SWR cache invalidation to reduce 13+ revalidation requests to 1 per operation.\n- Moves revalidation utilities from the chart app to `@openmrs/esm-patient-common-lib` for better reusability.\n- Creates multiple utility functions for surgical cache invalidation:\n  - `invalidateVisitHistory()` - Only invalidates visit history table data\n  - `invalidatePatientEncounters()` - Only invalidates encounter data\n  - `invalidateVisitAndEncounterData()` - Combines both for operations affecting both\n  - `useOptimisticVisitMutations()` - Hook for optimistic updates without network requests\n- Fixes the encounter table cache invalidation regex to handle flexible URL parameter order.\n- Updates all visit/encounter operations to use surgical cache targeting:\n  - Visit creation/editing (`visit-form.workspace.tsx`)\n  - Visit deletion/restoration (`useDeleteVisit.hook.tsx`)\n  - Encounter deletion (`encounters-table.component.tsx`)\n  - Form submissions (`form-entry.workspace.tsx`)\n  - Visit note creation (`visit-notes-form.workspace.tsx`)\n  - Order basket operations (`order-basket.workspace.tsx`)\n  - Vitals/biometrics forms (`vitals-biometrics-form.workspace.tsx`)\n  - End visit dialog (`end-visit-dialog.component.tsx`)\n- Preserves current visit component performance by avoiding unnecessary revalidation.\n- Ensures the `AllEncountersTable` updates correctly after form submissions and other encounter operations.\n\nThis eliminates the performance issue where visit CRUD operations triggered excessive network requests returning 304 responses, while maintaining proper data synchronization across all visit and encounter tables.\n\n* Make some tweaks and add test coverage","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"aa8fa4e1d33ea464ae981aba6314c0597588008e","date":"2025-06-16T19:44:22+03:00","message":"(BREAKING) Remove deprecated launchPatientWorkspace function (#2444)","refs":"","body":"* (test) Improve drug order test readability and assertions (#2483)\n\n* Review feedback","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b5e5e471987405a5588618e54d42667c4e83669c","date":"2025-06-13T20:56:03+03:00","message":"(chore) O3-4745: Fix failing dependency auto-update CI workflow (#2492)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":56}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LoCqtArF8WDKbCqKxvypH8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":